Wawacraft:Evolved version 0.3.12 [Satisfaction]

Wawacraft:Evolved is a free/libre 3D voxel-based
sandbox game with minimal features and maximal 
hack-ability.  It is written in C++, and uses C
libraries.

It can run on both Linux and Windows, and is 
intended to run on any platform following sane 
standards.  Your machine needs to have the 
following libraries available, GLFW, support 
C++, and OpenGL >=3.3

Wawacraft:Evolved is open to change, so if you
would like to contribute, please email me at 
<someguyshutup5@gmail.com> so we can work
together.

Wawacraft:Evolved is licensed under the GNU GPLv3 
License, and all its assets, (as found in the folders
archive and textures) are distributed under the 
CC-BY-SA 4.0 license, credited in authorship to
Ali Mohamed Ali (AKA the pseudonymous Stephen P. 
Hurlsmith).

Controls currently are:
WASD for movement
Arrow keys for rotation
Enter and Backspace for block editing
Tab for switching block types

Credits to libraries that I use in this project:
